r `jira-cloud-mutation-probe` to RUN vs SKIP) so the GREEN-live-run AC is reachable.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2","E6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2889,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Gated by `_live_jira_ready()` + `REBAR_RUN_EXTERNAL=1` + Cloud creds'","'export ... + REB Cloud env from secrets'","problem statement: read-only lane 'gated off (`vars.AWS_S3_REHEARSAL_ROLE_ARN` unset) — SKIPPED even in green runs'"],"finding":"The GREEN-live-run acceptance criterion depends on Jira Cloud credential secrets being provisioned in the repo, but the plan does not state this prerequisite. The problem statement notes the existing read-only Cloud lane is SKIPPED because `vars.AWS_S3_REHEARSAL_ROLE_ARN` is unset; the new lane is gated by 'Cloud creds' + REB Cloud env 'from secrets'. If those secrets are not provisioned, the new lane would likewise SKIP (enrolled in the all-skip canary) rather than run GREEN, so the AC could be unmet for a reason outside the code change.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbc6ef81ab2f40555","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"§2 gating / §3 lane / AC 'A dispatched Live External Integration run shows the new Cloud-mutation lane GREEN'","norm_id":"n7c246d932a006663","priority":0.8889,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The workflow is dispatched but Cloud secrets are absent, so the lane skips and the GREEN-run AC cannot be evidenced."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add a note enumerating the required secrets (REB Cloud base URL/token/project) and state that the GREEN-run AC presupposes they are configured; if absent, document that the lane skips via the all-skip canary rather than fails.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","cur